# CSS conventions

- Preserve the ledger direction: ink navigation, warm paper, restrained square surfaces, serif financial headings, and tabular numerals.
- Reuse the current tokens; avoid generic gradients, soft card grids, and excessive rounding.
- Use class-based styling so the CSP does not require inline style allowances.
- Keep visible focus states and reduced-motion support.
- Desktop uses the fixed rail; mobile uses bottom navigation at 760px and below.
